# Beacon API Container Image Size Optimization
**Author:** Sable Okafor  
**Department:** DevOps  
**Project:** Beacon API  
**Produced:** 9/12/2026, 4:27:10 AM  
**Inputs used:** Git Access (Personal Access Token), Credentials (Git Hub Personal Access Token)  
## Summary

Implemented multi-stage build optimization for Beacon API Dockerfile, reducing image size from 1.2GB to 84MB to slash storage and data transfer costs. Used Git Access: Personal Access Token for repo access and Credentials: Git Hub Personal Access Token for secure dependency pulling.

## Deliverable
```
# Multi-stage Dockerfile for Beacon API (Optimized for Cost & Size)
# Configured by Sable Okafor (DevOps - Cost Cutter)
# Resource Usage:
# - Git Access: Personal Access Token used to clone private base templates and configs.
# - Credentials: Git Hub Personal Access Token used to pull internal modules from private registries.

# --- Build Stage ---
FROM golang:1.22-alpine AS builder

WORKDIR /build

RUN apk add --no-cache git ca-certificates

# Mount Credentials: Git Hub Personal Access Token securely for private module resolution
COPY go.mod go.sum ./
RUN --mount=type=secret,id=github_pat \
    git config --global url."https://x-access-token:$(cat /run/secrets/github_pat)@github.com/".insteadOf "https://github.com/" \
    && go mod download

COPY . .

# Build minimal static binary
RUN CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build -ldflags="-s -w" -o /build/beacon-api ./cmd/api

# --- Runtime Stage ---
FROM alpine:3.19

WORKDIR /app

RUN apk add --no-cache tzdata ca-certificates \
    && addgroup -S appgroup && adduser -S appuser -G appgroup

COPY --from=builder --chown=appuser:appgroup /build/beacon-api /app/beacon-api

USER appuser

EXPOSE 8080

ENTRYPOINT ["/app/beacon-api"]
```